WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.070
In 1979, British trade unions
had 13.2 million members.

2
00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:10.860
In 2025, about 6.6 million
employees were members,

3
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.750
around 1 in 5.

4
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:16.550
Unions bargain with employers
for all their members at once.

5
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:18.980
Higher pay is often top of the list.

6
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.360
But if pay goes up,

7
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.970
will the employer hire fewer people?

8
00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:27.280
So can workers win higher pay
without anyone losing their job?

9
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.150
In this mission, you'll find
out what makes a union strong.

10
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.860
Then you'll draw what
happens when a union pushes

11
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.220
the wage above the market level.

12
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.810
Your mission: find out
when higher pay costs jobs,

13
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:40.910
and when it doesn't.
